From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 11:32:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04476/11362] [outer-loop] Verifier-gated-reasoning risk #2
 (headroom) FAILS gate at 9B -> full build moot for this model/corpus

Cheap headroom check before the large A/B/C build (phase-validation discipline):
does two-stage factual priming (the arXiv:2603.09906 mechanism) beat direct answer
for Qwen3.5-9B on SimpleQA-Verified? n=208, GPU 1, local LLM-judge applied
identically to both arms (replaces a substring matcher whose length bias favored
the verbose priming arm).

  acc(priming)=0.101 vs acc(direct)=0.077, delta +2.4pp, CI95 [-0.024,+0.072] -> STRADDLES 0.
  reasoning_headroom_confirmed=false.

The paper's recall effect (authors: Gemini-2.5 / Qwen3-32B) does NOT significantly
reproduce at 9B/single-hop. With no significant recall gain, a process verifier has
nothing to protect (C ~= B) -> the full A/B/C build is moot for this exact model+corpus
and is NOT built. #1 risk stays resolved-positive (verifier discriminates); #2 premise
failed the gate, saving the large build. Note updated (sec 4a/5) with revival conditions
(larger model / higher-headroom corpus).

